# lychee allow-list — broken links we accept on purpose.
#
# Each line is a regex matched against the FULL URL (lychee semantics).
# Add a comment explaining WHY before each pattern.

# (Retired 2026-08-14, v2.20 D7. The docs.rs entry for unpublished luna-*
# versions did what its own comment asked: it was removed once the crates
# shipped. Verified first — /luna-core/latest/, /luna-jit/latest/ and
# /luna-aot/2.18.0/ all return 200. Broken docs.rs links are now real
# failures again.)

# Font CDN origins referenced by `<link rel="preconnect">` in web/*.html.
# A preconnect target is a bare origin for the connection handshake, not a
# fetchable document — both return 404 for a plain GET, by design. The
# actual stylesheet URLs under fonts.googleapis.com/css2?... are checked
# normally.
^https://fonts\.googleapis\.com/?$
^https://fonts\.gstatic\.com/?$
